# Screenshots/docs
#
# These three lines have to stay in this order. A global ignore
# (~/.gitignore_global) excludes `docs` outright, and git never descends into an
# excluded directory — so any `!docs/...` exception below it is unreachable.
# Un-ignore the directory itself first, re-ignore its contents, then carve out
# the one subtree we want tracked.
#
# All three are anchored with a leading slash. Without it these match a `docs`
# directory at any depth, so `!docs/` also exposed backend/docs/ — which the
# global rule had been hiding.
!/docs/
/docs/*
# Design handoff: Claude Design reads this repo over GitHub, so the brief and
# the captured screens must be committed for it to see them at all.
!/docs/design-handoff/
.playwright-mcp/

# Scripts
scripts/restart-*.sh

# Pre-migration data snapshots (dumpdata backups) — local safety nets, not
# code; can contain real record data and shouldn't accumulate in history.
backend/scripts/backups/

# Docker data directories
docker/postgres/
docker/redis/
infrastructure/docker/postgres/
infrastructure/docker/redis/
